  {
   "post_number": 4,
   "username": "ZeptimusQ",
   "name": null,
   "created_at": "2022-05-24T19:38:44Z",
   "updated_at": "2022-05-24T19:38:44Z",
   "reply_to_post_number": null,
   "like_count": 0,
   "cooked": "<p>I guess we should really start <strong>focusing</strong> on the analysis and improve <strong>data accuracy</strong> having a dashboard is not enough to even suggest using this tool to reward people (from today’s stewards call). In my eyes this data is way worse than the old praise, how is even possible than in September before the commons upgrade Nuggan have 10x the value on Sem or 2x on Griff, using Nuggan who did an incredible work with the dashboard and all the community building with the debates just because he is the first one but the whole ladder looks pretty bad even looking at the bottom.</p>\n<p>I’m bullish on praise, but this is the second time I’m commenting the data is looking not so good and there is no so much feedback from people building it, but rather than we are analysing the data bla bla but every iteration we just post them wasting a learning opportunity to improve the tool we all love and want it to succeed. I know it’s hard to remember what happened on September but we could use more Advice process.</p>\n<p>Hope my words do not hurt anyone’s feelings  because the only intentions it’s to have a better system, Mutual monitoring, <img alt=\":male_detective:\" class=\"emoji\" src=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/images/emoji/win10/male_detective.png?v=10\" title=\":male_detective:\"/></p>",
   "action": null,
   "source": {
    "source": "commoncrawl",
