  {
   "post_number": 5,
   "username": "divine_comedian",
   "name": null,
   "created_at": "2022-05-26T15:28:06Z",
   "updated_at": "2022-05-26T15:54:08Z",
   "reply_to_post_number": null,
   "like_count": 2,
   "cooked": "<p>Zep looking at the data there’s a few things I notice using Sem as an example</p>\n<p></p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" data-download-href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/66d30a3fc17eb6ee32c18567f6d45e7e0d9b519b\" href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/original/1X/66d30a3fc17eb6ee32c18567f6d45e7e0d9b519b.png\" title=\"image\"><img alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"eFCQTBMoX8k6vRI1XJPXShnrYhl\" data-small-upload=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/optimized/1X/66d30a3fc17eb6ee32c18567f6d45e7e0d9b519b_2_10x10.png\" height=\"175\" src=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/optimized/1X/66d30a3fc17eb6ee32c18567f6d45e7e0d9b519b_2_690x175.png\" srcset=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/optimized/1X/66d30a3fc17eb6ee32c18567f6d45e7e0d9b519b_2_690x175.png, https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/optimized/1X/66d30a3fc17eb6ee32c18567f6d45e7e0d9b519b_2_1035x262.png 1.5x, https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/optimized/1X/66d30a3fc17eb6ee32c18567f6d45e7e0d9b519b_2_1380x350.png 2x\" width=\"690\"/><div class=\"meta\">\n<svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">image</span><span class=\"informations\">1824×465 193 KB</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg>\n</div></a></div>\n<p>This is from Round 3 - September 2021- The round is question.</p>\n<p>You can see we suffer from very low quality praise. The praise that was dished wasn’t very descriptive or was transcribed, implicitly not having a lot of context attached to it. Also Sem wasn’t really praised much.</p>\n<p>A few exceptional things we should consider:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>That we are retroactively quantifying praise from many months ago.</li>\n<li>The quantification process was still in active development, the quantifier pool had lots of new quantifiers when this was quantified.</li>\n<li>The highturn over of contributors means that many of the people who would have been in the know of something that happened in september aren’t involved in the TEC or quantification.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>I think that a few modifications like no longer transcribing praise, having better praise education, a smooth quantification process and onboarding and a clear praise dashboard UX will make a huge difference.</p>\n<p>ALSO we should consider that the sourcecred distribution isn’t included here but people who were active during this time will be accruing cred all the same, meaning when we disburse rewards for July we will have all the cred people like Sem and Livia accrued by their activity in Github and the Forum. We don’t quite have the full picture of all the value captured here which might be skewing our perspective.</p>\n<p>I’m up for some suggestions to improve praise, but let’s not forget the progress that has been made!</p>",
